;; levels are checked over, each with its pin. Milestone O1 (2026-10-30) records them; nothing of them is
;; in the tree: each is read from the release tarball fetched into .tmp/ and pinned by SHA-256 (OC10 (a)
;; authorizes the download), or in place (go-whim's whiml at a commit and a tree hash). Read with the Clojure
;; reader. Keys: :id; :what; :where (:pin a key of :pins, :paths under the tarball's top directory, or a
;; :root and :paths); :select (extensions counted; files of those extensions under :paths, recursively);
;; :files and :lines (the counts as of O1, every selected file, `wc -l` over their concatenation; `bin/repr-ocaml
;; corpus check` recomputes them); :ml and :mli (the split of :files); :license; :levels (the REAP cells it serves);
;; :until (the milestone that first reads it, survey §11). O7 adds the opam set: a pin :opam-NAME per package (:url, :sha256,
;; :sha512, :top, :license; fetched into .tmp/repr-ocaml/src/opam/ and extracted under .tmp/repr-ocaml/opam/NAME by `bin/repr-ocaml
;; corpus fetch`, read in place, not distributed) and a corpus :opam-NAME (OC101).
